# Documentation Standards for NetGrid

## Code Documentation
- Every public function, class, and module must have a docstring
- Use Google-style docstring format for consistency
- Include parameter types, return types, and examples
- Document exceptions that may be raised
- Keep docstrings concise but comprehensive

## README and User Documentation
- Keep README.md focused on user installation and usage
- Include clear installation instructions with virtual environment setup
- Provide usage examples with expected output
- Document all CLI options and their effects
- Keep user documentation in `docs/` directory

## Developer Documentation
- Maintain comprehensive project plans in `plans/` directory
- Document architecture decisions and rationale
- Keep technical specifications up to date
- Include setup instructions for development environment
- Document testing procedures and coverage requirements

## API Documentation
- Document all public interfaces clearly
- Include type hints for all function signatures
- Provide usage examples for complex functions
- Document data models and their relationships
- Keep API documentation in sync with implementation

## Planning Documents
- Update project status regularly in planning documents
- Track completed and pending features
- Document technical decisions and trade-offs
- Include performance benchmarks and targets
- Plan for future phases and features

## Code Comments
- Use comments to explain "why" not "what"
- Comment complex algorithms and business logic
- Explain non-obvious implementation details
- Keep comments up to date with code changes
- Use TODO comments for future improvements
